From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] skw: use GPIO descriptors

Drive the boot GPIOs through descriptors, which mainline requires since it
removed the OF integer GPIO lookups. A tree naming them as mainline does
(reset, host-wake, chip-wake) is read so; on a kernel that still has
of_get_named_gpio, a vendor tree's gpio_chip_en, gpio_host_wake and
gpio_chip_wake are read instead. Keep raw pin levels for the firmware
handshake. Numeric GPIO and debug overrides are refused. Propagate
acquisition errors from probe.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>

